From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Krapp <achterin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:25:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: turn off the LED of a stopped band

All bands of a mt7996 device share a single ieee80211_hw, so there is
only one mac80211 throughput LED trigger for all per-band LED classdevs.
The trigger's IEEE80211_TPT_LEDTRIG_FL_RADIO state is tracked per hw:
it is set when the first interface is opened and only cleared once the
whole hw is stopped. While any band is up, the trigger timer calls
led_trigger_blink() on every attached LED once per second, which switches
the hardware TX-blink mode back on for all bands.

As a result, disabling one radio leaves its LED lit as long as another
band is still running.

Keep the LED of a band that is not running off in the blink_set callback.
The trigger timer re-applies the blink settings every second, so the LED
of a stopped band goes dark on the next tick and stays off, without any
LED handling in the band start/stop paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Christoph Krapp <achterin@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/init.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/init.c
+++ b/mt7996/init.c
@@ -331,11 +331,22 @@ static int mt7996_led_set_blink(struct l
 				unsigned long *delay_on,
 				unsigned long *delay_off)
 {
+	struct mt76_phy *mphy = container_of(led_cdev, struct mt76_phy,
+					     leds.cdev);
 	u16 delta_on = 0, delta_off = 0;
 
 #define HW_TICK		10
 #define TO_HW_TICK(_t)	(((_t) > HW_TICK) ? ((_t) / HW_TICK) : HW_TICK)
 
+	/* The mac80211 throughput trigger is shared by all bands of the hw
+	 * and keeps blinking as long as any band is up. Keep the LED of a
+	 * band that is not running off instead of following the trigger.
+	 */
+	if (!test_bit(MT76_STATE_RUNNING, &mphy->state)) {
+		mt7996_led_set_config(led_cdev, 0, 0xff);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (*delay_on)
 		delta_on = TO_HW_TICK(*delay_on);
 	if (*delay_off)
